From 0d8324e7338d15d0ceb55ca43e888e61e44c62c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mehedi <growwithmh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:39:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove legacy inventory state and restrict task creation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The loader was only hiding the first half of startup. Two separate causes
remained underneath it.

Where the 94 came from
- inventory() fell back to a hardcoded five-category, 94-page plan whenever
  the project's own inventory was empty — including the whole window before
  the remote rows arrived, and any project that legitimately has none. That
  fallback is gone: in live mode an empty inventory is empty, and the seed
  list is reachable only when Supabase is not configured at all.
- The markup also shipped "/ 94 live" and a "Reset to 94" button.

Why it still flashed after the loader
- The shell had two owners. The gate dismissed it as soon as the session and
  profile resolved, which is well before the project rows land, so the app
  painted defaults for a frame. The shell now belongs to the app alone and
  lifts only once state is hydrated.

Atomic hydration
- render() is a no-op until state.hydrated. Every collection is staged first,
  assigned in one boundary, and only then is the view chosen and the first
  render performed. No tab is marked selected in the markup either, so
  nothing is highlighted before the saved view is known.
- The obsolete rmm-board-local-v2 cache is dropped after a live boot.

Inventory editing
- Baseline and draft are separate deep copies; the live inventory is never
  edited in place. Save writes and adopts the new baseline, Cancel writes
  nothing, Discard changes returns to the saved plan. There is no factory
  inventory to restore.

Task creation
- Owner and admin only, in the interface and in the database. Editors keep
  their existing rights over tasks they already have; creating and editing
  are separate permissions. A refused create explains itself rather than
  surfacing 42501.

One idempotent policy migration is required in production:
supabase/migrations/2026-09-13-owner-admin-task-creation.sql

146 tests passing.

